// Parity: assert_eq failure path.
//
// Sister test to assert_eq_success.tb. This program intentionally
// triggers an assert_eq failure so the parity harness exercises the
// rt_assert_eq_fail runtime helper's *failure* branch on both JIT and
// AOT — closing the test gap that the success-path test alone cannot
// cover.
//
// The parity harness picks up the sibling files
// `assert_eq_failure.expected_exit` (= 1) and
// `assert_eq_failure.expected_stderr` (substring of the diagnostic),
// and verifies BOTH the JIT and AOT runs:
//   * exit with status 1
//   * print the same diagnostic on stderr
//   * produce no stdout (the print after the failing assert is
//     unreachable)
fn main() {
    assert_eq(1, 2)
    print("unreachable")
}
